---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site, contact } from "@/data/siteConfig";

const licenseUrl = `${site.url}/works-license-v1`;
---
<LegalLayout title="Works License - V1" kicker="License">
  <h2>1. Application</h2>
  <p>
    This license applies to any work that includes a copy of it, states that it is licensed
    under it, or links to it. From that point, these terms govern how that work may be used.
    A work that neither includes nor links to this license is not covered by it.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>“The work”</strong> — the work covered by this license and copy of the work, in whole or in part, in
      any medium: written, printed, digital, audio, or video.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“The author”</strong> — the person or people credited as the original author of
      the work. In this case, the author is "Saif Bin Shahab".
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“You”</strong> — any person or organisation using the work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Modification”</strong> — any change to the work, including editing it,
      shortening or abridging it, adding to it, rearranging it or retitling it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>“Sharia'”</strong> — Islamic Law, as understood by a qualified Islamic Scholar.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What you are permitted to do</h2>
  <p>
    You may copy, distribute, redistribute, publish, sell, resell, print, store, and use the work in any
    way that Sharia' permits. The permission is deliberately broad: if Sharia' permits a use,
    this license permits it.
  </p>

  <h2>4. The conditions</h2>
  <h3>(a) Attribute the original author</h3>
  <p>
    Name the original author clearly wherever the work appears. Do not present the work as
    your own, and do not suggest that the author endorses you or your use of it.
  </p>

  <h3>(b) A copy of this license travels with the work</h3>
  <p>Every copy you distribute must include this license, in one of these forms:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>inside the work itself, or</li>
    <li>in printed form alongside the work, or</li>
    <li>
      a link or URL to this license:
      <a href={licenseUrl}>{licenseUrl}</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>(c) No modification</h3>
  <p>
    The work may not be changed. That includes editing it, shortening or abridging it, adding
    to it, rearranging it, retitling it, or presenting an altered version as
    the work. The one exception follows in Section 5.
  </p>

  <h2>5. The exception: modification for the greater good of The Muslim Ummah and people in general</h2>
  <p>
    If a modification genuinely serves the greater good of The Muslim Ummah and people in general, the work may be
    modified — but only in accordance with Sharia', with due attribution to the original author
    for the work, or for the part of the work that was used in the new work.
  </p>
  <p>
    That attribution must be clear and specific: name the original author, name the work
    used, and state what was changed. Conditions (a) and (b) above still apply to the
    modified work. This exception covers modification only; it does not remove the author's
    attribution, and it does not permit presenting the new work as entirely your own.
  </p>
  <p>
    Translation falls under this exception. As translations can be beneficial to The Muslim Ummah and people in general.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How to attribute</h2>
  <p>Attribution in any form is accptable provided that the work title and name of the author is mentioned and 
    the attribution is visible to the reader. An example is given below:</p>
  <blockquote class="not-italic">
    <p class="not-italic before:content-none after:content-none">
      Based on “[work title]” by [author name].<br />
      Used under Works License - V1 — <a href={licenseUrl}>{licenseUrl}</a>
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  <p>
    Place it where the work begins, on its credits or copyright page, or wherever it is
    clearly visible to the reader. For a modified work, add a line naming what was changed.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Selling and reselling</h2>
  <p>
    Selling and reselling the work is permitted at any price. What you may not do is claim
    authorship, place the work under a more restrictive license, or add conditions that
    contradict this one.
  </p>

  <h2>8. What this license does not cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party material inside a work — writings, quotations, images, logos, translations, software, codes 
      owned or authored by others, unless the owner or author of that third-party material explicitly put that
      material under this license.
    </li>
    <li>Any suggestion that the author endorses your use, product, or group.</li>
    <li>
      Religious rulings. This license is a permission between people, not a fatwa.
    </li>
    <li>Legal advice. Where the law grants you rights this license cannot change, they remain.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Versioning</h2>
  <p>
    This is version 1 (V1). A work published under V1 stays under V1, even if a later version
    appears; later versions apply only to works that say so. A copy distributed under V1 must
    carry V1 — linking to this page is enough.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Permission beyond this license</h2>
  <p>
    Permission for usage of the work is limited to what is mentioned in this license unless given explcit
    written permission by the author of the work.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you need a permission this license does not give, ask the author of the work first.
    For works published on this site:
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
